{
  "_source": "Hand-verified directly against RCA-DFC-REG-002.md SS27 per-field bit tables (0x3300-0x3324), cited by contract ID. LLINK_MONITOR_CONTROL/LLINK_QUALIFY_US/LLINK_TIMEOUT_US/LLINK_RECOVERY_US are each REG-002's own 'selected monitor' register, declared in indexed_registers (reggen.py v5, same mechanism RTL-014's session built, OPEN_ISSUES item 68) -- eight real stores each, written/read at LLINK_MONITOR_SELECT.MONITOR (REG-3308, REG-COH-001). The complete 8-monitor bank is forwarded to dfc_rtl015_control_t's new llink_monitor_m<0..7>__* fields (struct grown 128->961 bits this session) since RTL-015 must run all eight monitors simultaneously and continuously -- a single selected-view field cannot carry that. Each of these four registers' field list carries BOTH the struct's pre-existing selected-view fields (plain, driven by the indexed-register generator's own {name}_q selected-entry mux -- forwarded but functionally unused by dfc_rtl015.sv, item 73 precedent) AND the 8 new per-monitor array entries, since every bit of the control struct must be covered by exactly one field-map entry and reggen.py keys control_registers by register name (one dict entry per register, not two). rtl015_evt_overflow_status__event_overflow (14th EVENT_OVERFLOW-clear-field gap instance) was added in the same growth. LLINK_CONTROL/LLINK_MONITOR_SELECT/LLINK_ACTIVITY_INJECT are readback=internal_reg/zero; LLINK_STATUS/LLINK_ELAPSED_US/RTL015_EVT_OVERFLOW_STATUS are readback=external, closing the RTL-002/003/004-style host-READ gap (OPEN_ISSUES item 21) from the start.",
